WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.800
Give a PC12 cell the growth factor EGF, and it divides.

2
00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:13.820
Give the same cell NGF, and it stops dividing and grows long, nerve -like fibers.

3
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:21.200
Both signals run through the same four proteins: Ras, Raf, MEK and ERK.

4
00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:24.720
How can one chain of enzymes carry two instructions?

5
00:00:25.633 --> 00:00:29.973
At the membrane, SOS loads Ras with GTP, and Ras is on.

6
00:00:30.613 --> 00:00:33.393
Ras is not a kinase, so it works by contact.

7
00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:38.453
Active Ras catches Raf, a kinase that floats in the cytosol, folded shut.

8
00:00:39.293 --> 00:00:41.833
Binding brings Raf to the membrane, and there it opens.

9
00:00:42.593 --> 00:00:47.413
Then two Raf molecules pair, side by side, and pairing is needed for normal

10
00:00:47.413 --> 00:00:48.413
activation.

11
00:00:49.867 --> 00:00:54.427
Active Raf adds phosphates to the next kinase, mech, on two serines.

12
00:00:54.907 --> 00:00:56.407
Mech then does something unusual.

13
00:00:56.987 --> 00:01:02.207
It adds a phosphate to a threonine and another to a tyrosine, one residue apart, on

14
00:01:02.207 --> 00:01:04.087
ERK. ERK needs both.

15
00:01:04.587 --> 00:01:06.827
Take either one off, and ERK goes quiet.

16
00:01:08.617 --> 00:01:13.557
Negative feedback helps set how long the signal lasts, and ERK supplies its own.

17
00:01:14.077 --> 00:01:19.337
Active ERK phosphorylates proteins above it in the chain, among them SOS and Raf,

18
00:01:19.737 --> 00:01:20.917
and that weakens them.

19
00:01:21.317 --> 00:01:26.377
It also turns on genes for phosphatases, enzymes that take both phosphates back off

20
00:01:26.377 --> 00:01:31.417
ERK. That second kind of feedback is slower, because a protein has to be made.

21
00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:37.760
Different stimuli leave the pathway on for different lengths of time.

22
00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:45.280
In a PC -12 cell, ERK activity after EGF rises and falls back within about an hour.

23
00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:49.980
After NGF, it climbs to a plateau that lasts for hours.

24
00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:55.340
In 1992, Marshall's group proposed that this difference is itself the instruction.

25
00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:59.700
A brief signal goes with division, and a sustained one with differentiation.

26
00:02:00.933 --> 00:02:04.553
Now force MEK on for good, with no growth factor at all.

27
00:02:05.333 --> 00:02:10.093
ERK then stays on, which to a duration reader looks like a long NGF signal.

28
00:02:10.793 --> 00:02:17.873
In 1994, Cowley and Marshall did this, and PC -12 cells grew fibres with no NGF.

29
00:02:18.613 --> 00:02:24.313
One caution: this rule comes from one cell line, and how widely it holds is an open

30
00:02:24.313 --> 00:02:30.633
question. So keep this rule: in a PC -12 cell, how long ERK stays on carries the

31
00:02:30.633 --> 00:02:31.033
instruction.
